SEG = "RUL"
CAT = "fvicRules"
Q = [
    ("How many basic rules does the Victorian Firearm Safety Code set out?",
     "Ten", ["Eight", "Twelve", "Sixteen"],
     "The Victorian Firearm Safety Code, revised in 2020 by the Firearm Safety Foundation with Victoria Police, sets out ten basic rules of firearm safety."),
    ("Rule 10 says do not climb fences or obstacles with loaded firearms. The course slides define an obstacle as anything that:",
     "May make you lose muzzle control", ["Is higher than your waist", "Has barbed or electric wire", "Is on someone else's land"],
     "The longarm course slides say an obstacle is any situation that may cause you to lose control of the muzzle, so unload before negotiating it."),
    ("Under rule 2, the course slides define a safe direction as one where a discharge would cause no injury and:",
     "Little damage to property", ["No risk to livestock", "No damage to the firearm", "No shot leaving the property"],
     "The slides define a safe direction as one where, if the firearm went off, there would be no loss of life, no injury to anyone, and minimal damage to property."),
    ("Rule 9 says never fire at hard surfaces or water. Where does the booklet say to take special care?",
     "In rocky river beds", ["In long dry grass", "In thick timber", "On sandy ground"],
     "Rule 9 says ricochets can come off any flat or hard surface, such as rocks, snow, trees and water, and to be especially careful in rocky river beds."),
    ("Teaching rule 6, the instructors manual says safe storage matters even if your family knows the rules, because:",
     "Visitors may not know them", ["Police inspect at any time", "It lowers your insurance", "Theft voids your licence"],
     "The manual says an owner's family may be well aware of the safety rules, but visiting adults and children may not, so safe storage is essential."),
    ("Besides never firing at movement, colour, sound or shape alone, the course slides say which two things help identify a target?",
     "Size and location", ["Colour and movement", "Sound and shape", "Shape and colour"],
     "The slides for rule 4 say do not fire at movement, colour, sound or shape only, and that size and location also help you identify your target."),
    ("The booklet warns a firearm can go off unintentionally while you are:",
     "Releasing the safety catch", ["Removing the loaded magazine", "Lifting it from a case", "Fitting the sling"],
     "Rule 2 lists closing the action, releasing the safety catch, uncocking and opening a loaded firearm as moments it can fire unintentionally."),
    ("Under rule 3, when should you first load rounds into the magazine?",
     "At your shooting area", ["When you leave the car", "When you load the car", "When you first see game"],
     "Rule 3 says only load ammunition into the magazine when you have reached your shooting area, then carry the firearm with the bolt closed on an empty chamber."),
    ("Between shots while walking in your shooting area, rule 3 says a bolt action rifle should have:",
     "An empty chamber", ["A round chambered, safety on", "The bolt open and empty", "The magazine taken off"],
     "Rule 3 says unload the chamber when not firing a shot: put the round back in the magazine and close the bolt on an empty chamber."),
    ("With a self-loading rifle, the booklet suggests that once you acquire your target you load it and:",
     "Set the tested safety on", ["Keep it uncocked", "Leave the action open", "Rest a finger on the guard"],
     "Because rule 3 is not practical with self-loaders, the booklet recommends loading when you acquire your target and placing the previously tested safety catch on safe."),
    ("Before loading any round into the chamber of a self-loader, the booklet says to:",
     "Test the safety catch", ["Check the scope's zero", "Check the magazine spring", "Test the trigger pull"],
     "The booklet says test the safety catch before loading any rounds into the chamber, and if you have any doubt about it, have a gunsmith inspect it."),
    ("Under rule 4, the Code says you must not fire at a target identified by:",
     "Its sound alone", ["Its whole outline", "Size and location", "A clear view in daylight"],
     "Rule 4 says do not fire at movement only, colour only, sound only or shape only. The whole target must be identified beyond all doubt."),
    ("Before you shoot, the Code says to ask yourself which question?",
     "Is this a person?", ["Is this in season?", "Is this legal game?", "Is my backstop safe?"],
     "The booklet says asking 'Is this a person?' focuses your mind on expecting to see a person, rather than assuming it is an animal."),
    ("An unlicensed shooter fires under supervision. The booklet says who must positively identify the target?",
     "Both the shooter and supervisor", ["The supervisor alone", "The licence holder only", "Whoever fires the shot alone"],
     "Rule 4 in the booklet says the shooter, and anyone supervising an unlicensed shooter, must both positively identify the target."),
    ("The booklet says 'buck fever' is dangerous because a hunter may:",
     "See what they expect", ["Fire before aiming", "Forget the safety catch", "Lose track of companions"],
     "The booklet says tiredness or excitement can override rational thinking, so you may see what you expect to see, and objects, often people, can look like game."),
    ("Even the sight of hide and antlers is not enough, the booklet warns, because hunters have been shot while:",
     "Carrying a deer", ["Calling in game", "Dragging out a pig", "Wearing camouflage"],
     "The booklet says even a definite sighting of skin and antlers is not positive enough, since hunters have been shot while carrying a deer."),
    ("To scan the area for people before taking a shot, the booklet says to use:",
     "Binoculars", ["The rifle's scope", "A spotlight", "A camera zoom"],
     "The booklet says to identify targets with binoculars, not a rifle's telescopic sight, because the rifle may be loaded. Sweep the binoculars side to side to check no one is near your field of fire."),
    ("Which colour does the booklet recommend for all field shooting?",
     "Blaze orange", ["Bright red", "Fluorescent yellow", "Bright white"],
     "The booklet says blaze orange is the recommended colour for all field shooting, while reminding hunters that it only helps if others identify their targets."),
    ("Under rule 5, before firing the booklet says to ask yourself:",
     "What if I miss?", ["How far is my car?", "How many rounds are left?", "Is the target still moving?"],
     "Rule 5 says to be aware of what lies between you and the target and beyond it, and to ask what could happen if you miss."),
    ("The booklet says shooting at a target on the skyline is:",
     "Unsafe", ["Safe with a shotgun", "Safe on open farmland", "Safe with a backstop"],
     "The booklet lists a target on the skyline among targets never to shoot at, since the bullet's path beyond it cannot be seen and many hunting areas have homes nearby."),
    ("Two duck hunters share a hide. The booklet suggests driving vertical poles into the ground to:",
     "Stop an unsafe over-swing", ["Rest the shotguns on", "Steady each shooter's aim", "Hold the hide together"],
     "The booklet says duck shooters sharing a hide can drive vertical poles into the ground to prevent an over-swing endangering a companion."),
    ("Before leaving a shooting area, rule 3 says to unload completely, with no rounds in the magazine or chamber, and then:",
     "Double check it", ["Close the bolt on it", "Pull the trigger once", "Fit the safety catch"],
     "Rule 3 in the booklet says unload completely, with no rounds in the magazine or chamber, before leaving a shooting area or entering a hut or camp, and double check."),
    ("You see another shooter handling a firearm carelessly. The Firearm Safety Code booklet says you should:",
     "Give them safety advice", ["Leave the area quietly", "Report it to police later", "Tell the club afterwards"],
     "The booklet's safety guides say to give advice on safety if you see careless or unsafe behaviour with firearms, because irresponsible use causes injuries and deaths."),
    ("Teaching rule 8, the instructors manual says a large majority of firearm accidents happen:",
     "In or around the home", ["In vehicles on public roads", "At hunting camps", "In the field"],
     "The manual tells instructors to explain that a large majority of firearm accidents occur in or around the family home, so loaded firearms are never kept or taken there."),
    ("The instructors manual says a car's body and interior give what protection against bullets or shot?",
     "None", ["Some, from the doors", "Full, from the engine", "Some, from shotguns"],
     "The manual tells instructors to explain that car interiors and bodies do not offer protection against bullets or shot, so every firearm must be unloaded before entering any vehicle."),
    ("Rule 9 says never fire at hard surfaces or water. The booklet warns that when a ricochet occurs you have lost:",
     "Control of where it ends", ["The bullet's remaining energy", "Your shot's accuracy", "Sight of the target"],
     "Rule 9 says a ricochet means you have lost control of where the projectile will finish, which can injure another person or damage property."),
    ("The booklet says special care is needed when finishing off downed game birds:",
     "On water", ["In thick reeds", "On a muddy bank", "In standing crops"],
     "Rule 9 asks for extreme caution when dispatching downed game birds on water, because shot and bullets ricochet off water."),
    ("The course says to observe the Code, insist others do the same, and:",
     "Learn, practise and teach it", ["Sign and date it", "Report every breach", "Re-read it each new season"],
     "The course slides and manual end the ten rules with: observe this code; insist others do the same; learn, practise, teach and promote the firearm safety rules."),
]
